{"name":"Blue in the Face","hex":"#7b8fdf","fetched":"2026-10-23","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue in the face","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["For a hopelessly long time; used especially in respect to discussing, explaining, insisting, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue_in_the_face"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue in the Face","blocks":[{"text":"Blue in the Face is a 1995 American comedy film directed by Wayne Wang and Paul Auster. It stars Harvey Keitel leading an ensemble cast, including Giancarlo Esposito, Roseanne Barr, Michael J. Fox, Lily Tomlin, Victor Argo, Mira Sorvino, Lou Reed, Keith David, Jim Jarmusch, Jared Harris, RuPaul, and Madonna."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/75/Blue_in_the_face_ver1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_in_the_Face","wikidata":"Q2478977"},{"title":"Blue in the Face (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue in the Face is the second and final doubleDrive album, released in 2003. It sold 27,000 units in the US according to Soundscan. The album reached No. 43 on Top Heatseekers, and the single taken from the album, entitled \"Imprint\" reached No. 22 on Hot Mainstream Rock Tracks on Billboard charts."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fd/Doubledrive-Blue_in_the_Face.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_in_the_Face_(album)","wikidata":"Q4930102"},{"title":"Face","blocks":[{"text":"The face is \"the front part of the head of a human or other animal, featuring the eyes, nose and mouth, and the surrounding area.\" While that basic structure is found in many animals, the evolutionary development of mammals has led to a wide diversity of facial types between those species, identifiable by characteristics of facial features and expressive behaviors."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Human_faces.jpg/330px-Human_faces.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Face","wikidata":"Q37017"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/75/Blue_in_the_face_ver1.jpg/250px-Blue_in_the_face_ver1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/75/Blue_in_the_face_ver1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/75/Blue_in_the_face_ver1.jpg/250px-Blue_in_the_face_ver1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_in_the_face_ver1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fd/Doubledrive-Blue_in_the_Face.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fd/Doubledrive-Blue_in_the_Fac